`DEFAULT_I18N.addFilter` and `addFilterTitle` are now `''` in the shared Shade component. The default button renders `title={mergedI18n.addFilterTitle}` and `{addButtonText || mergedI18n.addFilter}`, so any consumer that doesn't override them now gets an icon-only button. It has no visible text, an empty `title`, and no `aria-label`.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="102-123"}

::code{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="2061-2076"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Screen readers will announce this as just "button". This is a design-system default, so the change also reaches the Storybook stories and any future `Filters` consumer, not just Stats.

Keep the library defaults. Have Stats opt into an icon-only button through props or i18n, and give the button an accessible name:

::suggestion{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="105-105"}
    addFilter: 'Add filter',

Then in `stats-filter.tsx`, pass something like `i18n={{addFilter: '', addFilterTitle: 'Add filter'}}`, or render a custom `addButton` with `aria-label="Add filter"`.

Operator values in this library use snake_case (`{value: 'is_any_of', label: i18n.operators.isAnyOf}`), and `addFilterWithOption` defaults multiselects to `'is_any_of'`. Here the Audience field passes the label string as the value:

::diff{file="apps/stats/src/views/Stats/components/stats-filter.tsx" lines="452-455"}

It only looks right because `FilterOperatorDropdown` can't find the value and falls back to `formatOperator`, which just replaces underscores. The stored `Filter.operator` is still the non-canonical `'is any of'`. Meanwhile the audience sync effect above (around line 293) rebuilds the filter with `operator: 'is'`, so the plain-text label switches between "is any of" and "is" depending on how the filter was created.

::suggestion{file="apps/stats/src/views/Stats/components/stats-filter.tsx" lines="453-453"}
                        defaultOperator: 'is_any_of',

You'll probably also want to change the sync effect's `operator: 'is'` to `'is_any_of'` so both paths agree.

This PR adds `setSearchInput('')` to `handleClose`, but it also removes the `handleClose()` call from the popover-mode single-select path:

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1274-1278"}

A programmatic `setOpen(false)` doesn't fire Radix's `onOpenChange`, so the `setTimeout(() => setSearchInput(''))` in `onOpenChange` never runs either. If you edit an applied single-select filter (such as the searchable "Post or page" field), search, and pick an item, the typed query is still there next time you open it. The selected-item branch a few lines up (around line 1240) still calls `setOpen(false); handleClose();`, so the two paths now behave differently.

::suggestion{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1275-1277"}
                                                    onChange([option.value] as T[]);
                                                    handleClose();

`newValues` was changed from `const` to `var` for no reason. It's never reassigned, `var` is function-scoped, and the Ghost TS lint preset normally flags it (`no-var`).

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1125-1125"}

::suggestion{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1125-1125"}
                                                    const newValues = [...effectiveValues, option.value] as T[];

`filters.length ? '' : ''` gives the same result on both sides. And because `''` is falsy, `Filters` falls back to `mergedI18n.addFilter` anyway. The only reason the button is icon-only is the library default change.

::diff{file="apps/stats/src/views/Stats/components/stats-filter.tsx" lines="497-498"}

Drop the prop and set the label and title through an `i18n` override, as described in the accessibility finding.

Tailwind's class is `animate-none`. `data-[state=closed]:!animation-none` generates no CSS, so only `!duration-0` takes effect. The same string is copied into three PopoverContent instances.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1201-1207"}

::suggestion{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1204-1204"}
                    'p-0 data-[state=closed]:!animate-none data-[state=closed]:!duration-0',

It would be cleaner to put this in one constant shared by the three call sites (lines 1204, 1644, 2081).
